00:40:19.950 --> 00:40:24.530
In fact, she was the first woman to direct a campaign for Bud Light.
事实上，她是第一位为百威淡啤执导广告战役的女性。

942
00:40:24.770 --> 00:40:25.890
I did not know that.
我以前不知道这一点。

943
00:40:26.090 --> 00:40:26.270
Yeah.
对。

944
00:40:26.290 --> 00:40:27.770
She's directed a bunch of commercials.
她导演过一堆广告。

945
00:40:28.050 --> 00:40:32.610
She's also won a Grammy as a member of Edward Sharp and the Magnetic Zeros.
她还作为爱德华·夏普与磁性零点乐队的成员赢得过格莱美奖。

946
00:40:32.910 --> 00:40:34.410
I really love this group.
我真的很喜欢这个乐队。

947
00:40:34.650 --> 00:40:38.370
You probably recognize their song, Home, which was a huge hit.
你们可能认出他们的歌《Home》，那是一首超级大热门。

948
00:40:38.550 --> 00:40:40.370
They were on all the talk shows.
他们上过所有的脱口秀节目。

949
00:40:40.610 --> 00:40:41.450
You want to hear it?
你想听听吗？

950
00:40:41.490 --> 00:40:41.670
Yes.
想听。

951
00:40:41.670 --> 00:40:42.450
I've got an audio clip.
我有一段音频剪辑。

952
00:40:42.830 --> 00:40:43.310
Okay.
好的。

953
00:40:43.390 --> 00:40:44.210
So this is the song.
就是这首歌。

954
00:40:44.290 --> 00:40:45.770
It opens with all the whistling.
一开场就是各种口哨声。

955
00:40:46.330 --> 00:40:46.810
Okay.
好的。

956
00:40:46.810 --> 00:40:47.630
Here's the whistling.
口哨声来了。

957
00:41:07.820 --> 00:41:09.140
I remember the whistling.
我记得这段口哨声。

958
00:41:09.140 --> 00:41:09.520
Yes.
没错。

959
00:41:09.680 --> 00:41:11.220
It just makes you happy right away.
它马上就能让你心情大好。

960
00:41:11.420 --> 00:41:12.120
It really does.
确实如此。

961
00:41:12.300 --> 00:41:15.780
And then here's, like, the chorus that you will remember as well.
然后这里是，比如，你也会记住的副歌。

962
00:41:42.720 --> 00:41:43.300
All right.
行吧。

963
00:41:43.380 --> 00:41:48.220
So that song got stuck in my head for about three days after I pulled that clip.
所以我截取这段音频后，这首歌在我脑子里盘旋了大约三天。

964
00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:49.560
It's just so catchy.
实在是太洗脑了。

965
00:41:49.820 --> 00:41:50.340
It's so catchy.
太洗脑了。

966
00:41:50.960 --> 00:41:53.100
Well, everyone, we reached out to Nora.
各位，我们联系了诺拉。

967
00:41:53.100 --> 00:41:55.920
We traded emails with her about her time on the show.
我们通过邮件和她交流了她在节目中的经历。

968
00:41:56.180 --> 00:41:59.120
Of course, we had to ask how she got her job on The Office,
当然，我们必须问她是怎么得到《办公室》这份工作的，

969
00:41:59.140 --> 00:42:03.560
and she said that she originally auditioned for Fanny, Dwight's sister.
她说她最初试镜的是德怀特的妹妹范妮。

970
00:42:03.560 --> 00:42:03.960
Oh.
哦。

971
00:42:04.280 --> 00:42:09.380
She said she remembers coming in a few times, and in one of the sessions, her and Rain improvised
她说她记得来试了好几次，在其中一场试镜中，她和雷恩

972
00:42:09.380 --> 00:42:11.700
a bit about various family-related matters.
即兴发挥了一些关于各种家庭琐事的内容。

973
00:42:11.960 --> 00:42:16.060
But after the audition, she heard they were thinking of her for something else and was
但在试镜后，她听说他们在考虑让她演别的角色，

974
00:42:16.060 --> 00:42:20.440
eventually told that she would be a potential love interest for Dwight on the farm.
最后被告知她将成为农场里德怀特的潜在恋爱对象。

975
00:42:21.200 --> 00:42:21.520
Yeah.
是啊。

976
00:42:21.520 --> 00:42:24.640
Maybe they had a little bit too much chemistry.
也许他们俩之间有点太有火花了。

977
00:42:25.080 --> 00:42:25.220
Yeah.
是啊。

978
00:42:26.180 --> 00:42:31.780
Nora also said she was a diehard fan of The Office and getting cast was a dream come true.
诺拉还说她是《办公室》的死忠粉，能参演简直是梦想成真。

979
00:42:32.100 --> 00:42:37.100
She also shared that it felt very fitting for it to be farm-related as she grew up in Iowa,
她还分享说，这和农场有关感觉非常合适，因为她是在艾奥瓦州长大的，

980
00:42:37.100 --> 00:42:40.520
and her dad was at one time in his life a corn farmer.
她父亲在一生中的某个时期曾是个玉米农场主。

981
00:42:40.720 --> 00:42:43.140
So she felt very at home with the storyline.
所以她对这个故事情节感到非常亲切。

982
00:42:43.360 --> 00:42:44.220
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

983
00:42:44.240 --> 00:42:44.900
I know.
就是说啊。

984
00:42:45.360 --> 00:42:45.680
Aw.
啊。

985
00:42:45.680 --> 00:42:51.360
Well, back at the grave site, Dwight shares that they've had some incidents of accidental
好了，回到墓地，德怀特分享说他们曾发生过意外活埋的事件，

986
00:42:51.360 --> 00:42:55.700
live burials, and grave robbers found scratch marks inside the coffin.
而且盗墓贼在棺材里发现了抓痕。

987
00:42:55.880 --> 00:42:58.920
So now, out of kindness, they take matters into their own hands.
所以现在，出于好意，他们决定亲自处理。

988
00:42:59.240 --> 00:43:03.720
That's when the minister tosses him a shotgun to make sure Aunt Shirley really is dead.
就在那时，牧师扔给他一把猎枪，以确保雪莉阿姨真的死了。

989
00:43:03.880 --> 00:43:04.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

990
00:43:04.400 --> 00:43:06.340
This is the breaking point for Oscar.
这对奥斯卡来说是崩溃的临界点。

991
00:43:06.520 --> 00:43:07.560
He's like, I'm out.
他心想，我可不干了。

992
00:43:07.560 --> 00:43:09.320
Yeah, Oscar's seen enough.
是啊，奥斯卡已经见识够了。

993
00:43:09.780 --> 00:43:14.640
Steve Burgess said that Rain had to do a test firing of the shotgun using blanks,
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，雷恩必须用空包弹对猎枪进行试射，

994
00:43:14.660 --> 00:43:17.100
and he had to go through safety training.
而且他还必须通过安全培训。

995
00:43:17.520 --> 00:43:20.380
He said we had our stunt coordinator, Brett Jones, on set.
他说我们的特技协调员布雷特·琼斯在片场。

996
00:43:20.580 --> 00:43:23.940
And, of course, Kelly, who he called the queen of safety meetings,
当然，他口中的安全会议女王凯利，

997
00:43:24.240 --> 00:43:27.500
held a giant safety meeting with the cast and crew before we shot that scene.
在拍摄那场戏之前，和演员及剧组人员开了一场盛大的安全会议。

998
00:43:27.740 --> 00:43:28.580
Kelly Cantley.
凯利·坎特利。

999
00:43:28.740 --> 00:43:29.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1000
00:43:29.340 --> 00:43:30.600
I love her safety meetings.
我太喜欢她的安全会议了。

1001
00:43:30.860 --> 00:43:32.400
This was a real safety meeting.
这真是一场真正的安全会议。

1002
00:43:32.700 --> 00:43:32.940
This was a real deal one.
这是一场来真的。

1003
00:43:32.940 --> 00:43:34.280
This was not lit candle.
这不是点燃的蜡烛。

1004
00:43:34.400 --> 00:43:35.000
This was not.
这不是。

1005
00:43:35.100 --> 00:43:36.880
We have three paper clips.
我们有三个回形针。

1006
00:43:36.880 --> 00:43:37.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1007
00:43:37.700 --> 00:43:39.260
That have been taken apart.
已经被拆散了。

1008
00:43:39.560 --> 00:43:40.720
They are pointy.
它们很尖锐。

1009
00:43:40.860 --> 00:43:41.520
They are pointy.
它们很尖锐。

1010
00:43:41.880 --> 00:43:47.220
I think the most dangerous thing that we had on our set of anything we had was the Death Star.
我认为我们在任何片场经历过的最危险的东西就是死星。

1011
00:43:47.320 --> 00:43:48.300
Of course it was.
当然是了。

1012
00:43:48.460 --> 00:43:53.240
That giant, giant metal-pronged star that hung from the ceiling.
那个从天花板上垂下来的巨大、布满金属刺的星星。

1013
00:43:53.340 --> 00:43:54.000
So low.
挂得那么低。

1014
00:43:54.220 --> 00:43:55.720
So low in Moroccan Christmas.
在摩洛哥圣诞节里挂得那么低。

1015
00:43:56.020 --> 00:43:56.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1016
00:43:56.440 --> 00:43:56.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1017
00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:57.700
You know why?
你知道为什么吗？

1018
00:43:57.800 --> 00:43:59.260
Because it was a sneaky danger.
因为它是一种潜藏的危险。

1019
00:43:59.740 --> 00:44:01.300
We didn't see that one coming.
我们完全没料到那个。

1020
00:44:01.480 --> 00:44:02.220
Sneaky danger.
潜藏的危险。

1021
00:44:02.520 --> 00:44:02.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1022
00:44:03.420 --> 00:44:05.520
Sneaks up on you, and you walk into it.
悄悄靠近你，然后你一头撞上去。

1023
00:44:06.280 --> 00:44:06.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1024
00:44:09.290 --> 00:44:09.790
Okay.
好啦。

1025
00:44:11.070 --> 00:44:12.990
We are back in the conference room.
我们回到了会议室。

1026
00:44:13.430 --> 00:44:17.710
Pam is really insisting to everyone that they cannot eat these cupcakes.
帕姆极力向所有人强调他们不能吃这些纸杯蛋糕。

1027
00:44:17.950 --> 00:44:19.750
Packer cannot buy their forgiveness.
帕克买不到他们的原谅。

1028
00:44:20.490 --> 00:44:23.290
This is when we learned that Creed is really great with numbers.
这就是我们发现克里德对数字非常敏感的时候。

1029
00:44:23.590 --> 00:44:26.970
I mean, he forgets literally everything else, but he has a gift with numbers.
我是说，他 literalmente 记不住别的任何事，但他对数字有着非凡的天赋。

1030
00:44:26.970 --> 00:44:29.650
And that's why he's an accountant, which he is not.
这就是为什么他是一名会计，虽然他根本不是。

1031
00:44:30.050 --> 00:44:30.810
That's right.
没错。

1032
00:44:31.150 --> 00:44:34.330
None of us really know what Creed does, and clearly Creed does not either.
我们谁也不知道克里德到底是干什么的，显然克里德自己也不知道。

1033
00:44:34.950 --> 00:44:39.770
Clark and Todd Packer, who are sitting out at the desks, they're not in the conference room,
克拉克和托德·帕克坐在外面的办公桌旁，他们没有进会议室，

1034
00:44:40.110 --> 00:44:41.210
are going to have a moment.
接下来他们要有一段互动了。

1035
00:44:41.490 --> 00:44:45.390
Todd's going to apologize to Clark for calling him a fat little runt.
托德要为之前叫克拉克“胖墩小侏儒”向他道歉。

1036
00:44:46.110 --> 00:44:48.530
Clark tells Todd, you did not call me that.
克拉克告诉托德，你才没那么叫过我。

1037
00:44:49.050 --> 00:44:53.290
And Todd Packer says, well, I'm just in the habit of apologizing for thoughts I had in my head.
然后托德·帕克说，好吧，我只是习惯为我脑子里闪过的想法道歉。

1038
00:44:53.290 --> 00:44:54.810
He gives Clark a cupcake.
他给了克拉克一个纸杯蛋糕。

1039
00:44:55.450 --> 00:44:57.610
Stanley really wants to eat the cupcakes.
斯坦利真的很想吃纸杯蛋糕。

1040
00:44:58.350 --> 00:45:00.610
He's really making a case for it.
他正在极力为吃这个找理由。

1041
00:45:00.750 --> 00:45:03.470
Yeah, he said, you know, we've done some stuff to Packer.
对，他说，你知道的，我们对帕克做过不少事。

1042
00:45:03.590 --> 00:45:05.450
Like, we sent him to Florida on a prank.
比如，我们恶作剧把他骗去了佛罗里达。

1043
00:45:05.850 --> 00:45:06.890
Nellie's like, that's true.
奈莉说，这倒也是。

1044
00:45:06.890 --> 00:45:07.930
And I fired him.
而且我还开除过他。

1045
00:45:07.930 --> 00:45:10.990
They're all trying to justify eating these cupcakes.
他们都在试图为吃这些纸杯蛋糕找借口。

1046
00:45:11.390 --> 00:45:15.310
Well, people like cupcakes, Ange, and that's why I brought them in for your birthday.
好吧，人们都喜欢纸杯蛋糕，安吉，这就是为什么我为你过生日把它们带进来了。

1047
00:45:15.530 --> 00:45:15.950
I know.
我知道。

1048
00:45:15.950 --> 00:45:17.390
I really want to have some.
我真的很想吃几个。

1049
00:45:17.550 --> 00:45:18.810
They're sitting right in front of me.
它们就摆在我面前。

1050
00:45:18.930 --> 00:45:23.130
Well, now would be a good time because I also asked you your favorite cupcake flavors
好吧，现在正是时候，因为我还问过你最喜欢的纸杯蛋糕口味是什么呢

1051
00:45:23.130 --> 00:45:25.890
for another reason, not just for your birthday.
为了另一个原因，不只是为了你的生日。

1052
00:45:26.030 --> 00:45:27.550
Does this say something about you?
这能说明你什么吗？

1053
00:45:27.650 --> 00:45:30.550
Or am I now going to find out that I'm just basic?
还是说我等会儿就要发现自己其实是个很俗气的人？

1054
00:45:31.030 --> 00:45:31.470
Yes.
是的。

1055
00:45:31.870 --> 00:45:33.730
Ange, you've ruined the surprise.
安琪，你把惊喜给剧透了。

1056
00:45:34.010 --> 00:45:34.710
I'm sorry.
对不起。

1057
00:45:34.710 --> 00:45:38.670
I found an article on SpoonUniversity.com.
我在 SpoonUniversity.com 上看到一篇文章。

1058
00:45:38.930 --> 00:45:42.650
What does your favorite cupcake flavor say about you?
你最喜欢的纸杯蛋糕口味说明了什么？

1059
00:45:42.790 --> 00:45:43.250
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1060
00:45:44.330 --> 00:45:44.710
All right.
好吧。

1061
00:45:44.810 --> 00:45:45.330
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

1062
00:45:46.010 --> 00:45:50.990
Angela, when I asked you what kind of cupcake you like, you said vanilla.
安吉拉，当我问你喜欢什么口味的纸杯蛋糕时，你说的是香草味。

1063
00:45:52.570 --> 00:45:57.130
And that means you are, quote, the boring friend who doesn't know how to text.
这意味着，引用原话说，你是个连发短信都不会的无聊朋友。

1064
00:45:58.190 --> 00:46:00.670
F*** you, SpoonUniversity.com.
去你的，SpoonUniversity.com。

1065
00:46:01.590 --> 00:46:03.010
But not wrong.
但也没说错。

1066
00:46:03.830 --> 00:46:05.450
I know how to text.
我会发短信。

1067
00:46:05.730 --> 00:46:07.270
What is wrong with my texting?
我的短信怎么了？

1068
00:46:07.430 --> 00:46:08.810
And I am anything but boring.
而且我绝对谈不上无聊。

1069
00:46:09.150 --> 00:46:14.370
Well, this is true, but it goes on to say, unfortunately, Angela, you're unoriginal.
好吧，这倒不假，但文章接着说，不幸的是，安吉拉，你没有什么创意。

1070
00:46:14.690 --> 00:46:15.650
But it's okay.
不过没关系。

1071
00:46:15.770 --> 00:46:17.350
It says it's okay.
上面说没关系。

1072
00:46:17.450 --> 00:46:21.270
We're all a little unoriginal and like to stick to the basics sometimes.
我们多多少少都有点缺乏创意，有时就喜欢追求最基本的东西。

1073
00:46:22.110 --> 00:46:25.910
If this is your classic cupcake order, you just like simplicity.
如果这是你点纸杯蛋糕的经典选择，说明你就是喜欢简单。

1074
00:46:26.370 --> 00:46:30.190
I wish my life was as easy as this cupcake, is what you're saying.
你的意思是，希望我的生活能像这个纸杯蛋糕一样简单。

1075
00:46:30.190 --> 00:46:34.470
You crave simplicity, so you keep it simple with your cupcakes.
你渴望简单，所以在纸杯蛋糕上也保持简单。

1076
00:46:34.750 --> 00:46:37.130
I'm sorry, but unoriginal.
对不起，但说我缺乏创意。

1077
00:46:38.390 --> 00:46:40.430
Sounds like someone's throwing shade.
听起来好像有人在阴阳怪气。

1078
00:46:41.630 --> 00:46:42.370
I'm sorry.
对不起。

1079
00:46:42.470 --> 00:46:43.450
This is just what it said.
这上面就是这么写的。

1080
00:46:44.490 --> 00:46:50.130
Cassie, you said in your email that you do not love cupcakes, which is very on brand for you.
凯西，你在邮件里说你不太喜欢纸杯蛋糕，这非常符合你的风格。

1081
00:46:50.250 --> 00:46:53.550
But when forced to choose, you chose red velvet.
但当被迫做出选择时，你选了红丝绒。

1082
00:46:54.630 --> 00:46:58.930
This means that you are, quote, the one who's going to grow up to be a surgeon.
这意味着，引用原话说，你将来会成为一名外科医生。

1083
00:46:59.570 --> 00:46:59.770
What?
什么？

1084
00:47:01.450 --> 00:47:04.110
Spoon University is full of shit.
Spoon University 完全是在胡扯。

1085
00:47:04.430 --> 00:47:04.670
Those two are so different.
这两者差得也太远了。

1086
00:47:04.990 --> 00:47:05.330
I know.
我知道。

1087
00:47:05.790 --> 00:47:09.430
It says, red velvet cupcakes mean business.
上面说，红丝绒纸杯蛋糕代表着认真干实事。

1088
00:47:09.430 --> 00:47:12.370
You're slick and smooth and well-dressed.
你精明圆滑、衣着光鲜。

1089
00:47:12.590 --> 00:47:18.450
That moist cupcake and cream cheese frosting mesh together so well, just like your life seems to.
那湿润的蛋糕和奶油奶酪糖霜完美融合，就像你看似顺风顺水的生活一样。

1090
00:47:18.450 --> 00:47:20.870
Can we, Cassie, will you just say what you're wearing today?
凯西，我们能……你能不能说说你今天穿的是什么？

1091
00:47:21.090 --> 00:47:21.490
Yeah.
好吧。

1092
00:47:21.750 --> 00:47:24.810
I'm wearing slides and basketball shorts.
我穿着拖鞋和篮球短裤。

1093
00:47:24.970 --> 00:47:27.870
I am, like, the worst dressed one today.
我今天简直可以说是穿得最差的一个了。

1094
00:47:29.610 --> 00:47:31.390
Not according to your cupcake.
你的纸杯蛋糕可不这么认为。

1095
00:47:32.070 --> 00:47:32.490
All right.
好吧。

1096
00:47:32.870 --> 00:47:36.510
Sam and I both chose chocolate with vanilla frosting.
我和萨姆都选了巧克力配香草糖霜。

1097
00:47:37.390 --> 00:47:37.950
Sam.
萨姆。

1098
00:47:38.190 --> 00:47:38.510
Okay.
好吧。

1099
00:47:38.710 --> 00:47:41.030
You and I are, quote, the fake hipster.
你和我属于，引用原话说，虚假文青。

1100
00:47:41.330 --> 00:47:41.570
Okay.
好吧。

1101
00:47:42.070 --> 00:47:42.370
Damn.
该死。

1102
00:47:42.650 --> 00:47:45.050
Spoon University hates all of us.
Spoon University 恨我们所有人。

1103
00:47:45.110 --> 00:47:46.290
Who runs this site?
这网站谁开的？

1104
00:47:46.290 --> 00:47:47.550
Okay, it's...
好吧，是……

1105
00:47:47.550 --> 00:47:49.710
Jenna, do you run Spoon?
珍娜，Spoon 是你运营的吗？

1106
00:47:49.890 --> 00:47:50.710
No, I do not.
不，不是我。

1107
00:47:50.810 --> 00:47:51.730
I do not.
真不是我。

1108
00:47:51.890 --> 00:47:53.250
But here's what it says.
但它是这么写的。

1109
00:47:53.430 --> 00:48:00.010
It says, if a chocolate cupcake with vanilla frosting is a regular in your diet, you're probably pretty basic, too.
上面说，如果香草糖霜巧克力纸杯蛋糕是你的常备日常饮食，那你大概也挺烂大街的。

1110
00:48:00.330 --> 00:48:00.750
Jesus.
天哪。

1111
00:48:01.490 --> 00:48:05.570
You just get the chocolate cupcake to pretend you're more edgy.
你买巧克力纸杯蛋糕只是为了假装自己很另类。

1112
00:48:05.630 --> 00:48:06.910
Who hurt this person?
这人受过什么情伤吧？

1113
00:48:07.070 --> 00:48:07.570
I don't know.
我不知道。

1114
00:48:07.630 --> 00:48:10.850
I think whoever wrote this doesn't like anyone.
我觉得写这东西的人谁都看不惯。

1115
00:48:11.150 --> 00:48:11.410
Yeah.
就是。

1116
00:48:11.530 --> 00:48:11.690
Yeah.
对啊。

1117
00:48:12.630 --> 00:48:13.290
All right.
好吧。

1118
00:48:13.530 --> 00:48:19.470
Now, Sam, in your email, you were trying to decide between chocolate with vanilla frosting and Oreo.
萨姆，你在邮件里提到，你当时在香草糖霜巧克力和奥利奥之间纠结。

1119
00:48:19.690 --> 00:48:20.170
Yeah, that's right.
对，没错。

1120
00:48:20.510 --> 00:48:23.150
Angela, is there any chance you would go Oreo?
安吉拉，你会有可能选奥利奥吗？

1121
00:48:23.490 --> 00:48:23.830
No.
不会。

1122
00:48:24.650 --> 00:48:25.130
Okay.
好吧。

1123
00:48:25.590 --> 00:48:25.950
No.
绝不。

1124
00:48:26.130 --> 00:48:29.830
Oreo is, quote, the one who writes in a diary.
奥利奥是那种，引号里说的，会写日记的人。

1125
00:48:31.470 --> 00:48:31.950
Okay.
好吧。

1126
00:48:33.010 --> 00:48:34.670
Oh, Sam, how's your diary?
哦，萨姆，你的日记写得怎么样了？

1127
00:48:35.070 --> 00:48:35.790
Honestly, good.
说实话，挺好的。

1128
00:48:36.310 --> 00:48:37.390
Well, here's the way.
行吧，它是这么说的。

1129
00:48:37.430 --> 00:48:41.070
If you choose Oreo, it says, you're a bit of a piece of work.
如果你选奥利奥，上面说，你这人挺难搞的。

1130
00:48:41.410 --> 00:48:43.170
From the outside, you're sweet.
从外表看，你人很好。

1131
00:48:43.350 --> 00:48:44.370
I mean, who wouldn't be?
我的意思是，谁不是呢？

1132
00:48:44.510 --> 00:48:48.950
But once people dig deep enough, they'll find out you've got some very profound secrets.
但只要别人深入了解，就会发现你藏着不少不可告人的秘密。

1133
00:48:49.270 --> 00:48:50.450
Are any of these good?
这里面有哪个是好话吗？

1134
00:48:50.570 --> 00:48:50.970
Yeah.
有啊。

1135
00:48:51.210 --> 00:48:52.910
Well, I'll tell you what.
这样吧。

1136
00:48:53.070 --> 00:48:53.710
I'll tell you what.
我跟你说。

1137
00:48:53.710 --> 00:48:55.110
I'm going to end with this one because...
我打算用这个作结，因为……

1138
00:48:55.690 --> 00:48:56.370
Is it lemon?
是柠檬味吗？

1139
00:48:56.510 --> 00:48:57.650
Because I also love lemon.
因为我也很喜欢柠檬。

1140
00:48:57.850 --> 00:48:58.530
It's lemon!
是柠檬！

1141
00:48:58.850 --> 00:49:00.070
Oh, that was the one.
哦，就是这个。

1142
00:49:00.150 --> 00:49:02.170
I didn't say that one because I love lemon.
我没选那个可不是因为我喜欢柠檬。

1143
00:49:02.170 --> 00:49:02.830
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1144
00:49:03.050 --> 00:49:03.730
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1145
00:49:03.730 --> 00:49:05.910
So, I almost picked lemon.
所以，我差一点就选柠檬了。

1146
00:49:06.150 --> 00:49:10.250
If the bakery where I got our cupcakes would have had lemon, I would have gotten lemon.
如果买纸杯蛋糕的那家店有柠檬味的话，我肯定就买柠檬的了。

1147
00:49:10.270 --> 00:49:11.070
I love lemon.
我超爱柠檬。

1148
00:49:11.310 --> 00:49:14.370
But it didn't, so I had to go with the chocolate with vanilla frosting.
但他们没有，所以我只能选了香草糖霜巧克力。

1149
00:49:14.390 --> 00:49:18.390
Yeah, vanilla's like, I'll take vanilla, but if there's lemon, I'll almost always pick it.
对啊，香草这种口味吧，我是会吃，但如果有柠檬，我几乎每次都会选柠檬。

1150
00:49:18.470 --> 00:49:19.610
But there's usually not.
不过通常都没有。

1151
00:49:19.930 --> 00:49:20.830
Okay, well.
好吧，那个。

1152
00:49:21.070 --> 00:49:21.450
Uh-oh.
噢噢。

1153
00:49:22.610 --> 00:49:28.590
Lemon is, quote, the one who hates 90% of the friend group but pretends to love all of them.
柠檬引用原话说：“她是那种讨厌朋友圈里90%的人，却假装爱所有人的人。”

1154
00:49:30.900 --> 00:49:36.740
This is the take on cupcakes.
这就是对纸杯蛋糕的看法。

1155
00:49:36.740 --> 00:49:40.780
Someone was dumped by a cupcake or someone was broken up with by a cupcake.
有人被纸杯蛋糕甩了，或者有人被纸杯蛋糕给分了手。

1156
00:49:41.400 --> 00:49:42.380
Here's what it says.
上面是这么写的。

1157
00:49:42.540 --> 00:49:47.200
If you're eating a lemon cupcake, it says, you've got an attitude no one can quite understand.
如果你在吃柠檬纸杯蛋糕，上面说，你有一种让人捉摸不透的态度。

1158
00:49:48.540 --> 00:49:53.020
Everyone loves you, but you're a little bit less sweet and loving than everyone else is.
每个人都爱你，但你比其他人少了一点甜美和爱意。

1159
00:49:53.140 --> 00:49:53.760
It's okay.
没关系。

1160
00:49:54.260 --> 00:49:56.520
Sometimes it's hard to love crazy bitches.
有时要爱那些疯狂的碧池很难。

1161
00:49:57.560 --> 00:49:58.040
Whoa!
哇哦！

1162
00:49:58.740 --> 00:49:59.820
So, what am I?
那么，我是什么？

1163
00:49:59.960 --> 00:50:02.380
Am I unoriginal or am I a crazy bitch?
我是毫无新意，还是个疯狂的碧池？

1164
00:50:02.560 --> 00:50:03.540
Maybe a little about...
也许有点关于……

1165
00:50:03.540 --> 00:50:04.020
I'm a, like...
我大概是个……

1166
00:50:04.020 --> 00:50:04.720
A little column A?
A栏有一点？

1167
00:50:04.900 --> 00:50:05.680
A little column B.
B栏也有一点。

1168
00:50:07.280 --> 00:50:08.480
Well, there you have it.
好了，答案就在这儿了。

1169
00:50:08.620 --> 00:50:10.980
That's what your cupcake choice says about you.
这就是你选择的纸杯蛋糕所体现的你。

1170
00:50:11.320 --> 00:50:14.360
Spoon University is a harsh place.
勺子大学可真是个严苛的地方。

1171
00:50:15.580 --> 00:50:15.980
Damn.
靠。

1172
00:50:16.640 --> 00:50:17.940
Can I have my cupcake now?
我现在能吃我的纸杯蛋糕了吗？

1173
00:50:18.720 --> 00:50:19.120
Sure.
当然。

1174
00:50:20.320 --> 00:50:21.580
Dig in, everybody.
大家开吃吧。

1175
00:50:23.060 --> 00:50:26.720
Well, lady, I will say, you and I both love lemon cupcakes, so what does that say?
好吧，女士，我要说，你和我都很喜欢柠檬纸杯蛋糕，那这说明什么？

1176
00:50:26.900 --> 00:50:28.780
I guess we're a couple of crazy bitches.
我猜我们俩都是疯狂的碧池。

1177
00:50:28.920 --> 00:50:29.420
I guess so.
我想是的。

1178
00:50:30.440 --> 00:50:30.980
All right.
好吧。

1179
00:50:31.080 --> 00:50:33.120
Well, now we're going to go back to Aunt Shirley's house.
那么，现在我们要回到雪莉阿姨家。

1180
00:50:33.460 --> 00:50:36.540
Her family has gathered to watch a farewell video.
她的家人聚在一起观看告别视频。

1181
00:50:37.200 --> 00:50:38.280
It's like her will?
就像她的遗嘱一样？

1182
00:50:38.900 --> 00:50:39.300
Yes.
是的。

1183
00:50:39.700 --> 00:50:40.720
I wrote this.
这个是我写的。

1184
00:50:40.840 --> 00:50:45.760
I did not play a bullsh** card here, but I would like to say that this video lays a lot of pipe.
我在这里没有打胡扯牌，但我想说，这个视频铺垫了很多内容。

1185
00:50:46.600 --> 00:50:49.540
Well, we also had to reshoot this video.
好吧，我们还得重新拍摄这个视频。

1186
00:50:49.890 --> 00:50:52.000
We mentioned this during Moving On.
我们在《继续前行》里提到过这个。

1187
00:50:52.280 --> 00:50:57.140
There was originally a different woman cast as Aunt Shirley in the pilot of the farm,
最初在试播集中，农场里扮演雪莉阿姨的演员是另一个人，

1188
00:50:57.140 --> 00:51:01.600
and this was the only thing that that actress had to do was just read this will.
而那个女演员唯一要做的事就是念这段遗嘱。

1189
00:51:01.600 --> 00:51:08.680
But when they wrote Moving On and they expanded the role, they cast just legendary character
但当他们写了《继续前行》并扩展了这个角色后，他们换上了传奇性格

1190
00:51:08.680 --> 00:51:10.680
actress Mary Gillis in the role.
女演员玛丽·吉利斯来扮演这个角色。

1191
00:51:10.920 --> 00:51:16.740
Well, this video sets up the whole entire series if it would have gone.
好吧，如果这个系列能拍下去的话，这个视频为整个系列做好了铺垫。

1192
00:51:16.960 --> 00:51:17.660
Listen to this.
听听这个。

1193
00:51:18.120 --> 00:51:19.540
Aunt Shirley on the video says,
视频里的雪莉阿姨说，

1194
00:51:19.680 --> 00:51:21.360
Thank you for coming to my funeral.
谢谢你们来参加我的葬礼。

1195
00:51:21.720 --> 00:51:25.940
As I gaze at life's big sunset, I can't help but wonder where it all went wrong.
当我凝视着生命的大落日时，我不禁纳闷这一切是从哪里开始出错的。

1196
00:51:26.120 --> 00:51:27.980
You've all disappointed me greatly.
你们所有人都让我大失所望。

1197
00:51:28.320 --> 00:51:30.420
Fanny, a single mama in the city.
范妮，城里的单亲妈妈。

1198
00:51:30.900 --> 00:51:32.600
Fanny, Jeb, a street pusher.
范妮，杰布，街头小贩。

1199
00:51:32.800 --> 00:51:39.040
And so we find out that Jeb has a nine-acre worm farm, which turns out worm means marijuana.
然后我们发现杰布有一个九英亩的“虫子农场”，结果证明虫子指的是大麻。

1200
00:51:39.320 --> 00:51:41.240
And then Aunt Shirley ends it with,
然后雪莉阿姨以这句话结束：

1201
00:51:41.480 --> 00:51:45.260
We can't just sit by and watch our family farm disappear, so here are my terMs.
我们不能坐视我们的家庭农场消失，所以这是我的条件。

1202
00:51:45.540 --> 00:51:49.400
Dwight, Fanny, and Jeb, if you come back home, I will leave you my farm.
德怀特、芬妮和杰布，如果你们回家，我就把农场留给你们。

1203
00:51:49.580 --> 00:51:51.140
So there, you have it.
就是这样，你们知道了。

1204
00:51:51.280 --> 00:51:56.660
So in this one video, we learn what the whole entire premise of the series is going to be.
所以通过这一个视频，我们了解了整个剧集的全部设定是什么。

1205
00:51:56.660 --> 00:52:03.820
Yes, we also learned earlier that Aunt Shirley's farm is, I guess, adjacent to Dwight's farm.
是的，我们之前也了解到雪莉阿姨的农场，我猜，就在德怀特农场的隔壁。

1206
00:52:04.100 --> 00:52:07.480
So they would have Dwight's farm and this farm, and they'd have all that land.
所以他们会拥有德怀特的农场和这个农场，他们将拥有所有这些土地。

1207
00:52:07.840 --> 00:52:09.720
We now have two talking heads.
我们现在有两个访谈镜头。

1208
00:52:10.100 --> 00:52:11.740
Jeb has a talking head and then Dwight.
杰布有一个访谈镜头，然后是德怀特。

1209
00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:14.180
There are two talking head locations on the farm.
农场上有两个访谈镜头的取景地。

1210
00:52:14.320 --> 00:52:17.900
You're either in the porch swing or you're in the rocking chair on the porch.
你要么坐在门廊的秋千上，要么坐在门廊的摇椅上。

1211
00:52:17.900 --> 00:52:19.660
Oh, nice catch.
哦，眼力真好。

1212
00:52:20.440 --> 00:52:25.620
If you watch the talking heads in the rocking chair, Dwight has one and Zeke has one later,
如果你看坐在摇椅上的访谈，德怀特有一个，后来泽克也有一个，

1213
00:52:25.840 --> 00:52:28.320
you will see a blue Weber grill in the background.
你会看到背景里有一个蓝色的韦伯烤炉。

1214
00:52:28.640 --> 00:52:28.880
Oh.
哦。

1215
00:52:29.380 --> 00:52:30.320
Isn't that so random?
是不是觉得很随性？

1216
00:52:30.620 --> 00:52:33.060
Like a Weber grill, you know, with the lid that you lift up?
就像韦伯烤炉那样，你知道的，带有可以掀开的盖子？

1217
00:52:33.240 --> 00:52:33.500
Yeah.
对。

1218
00:52:33.860 --> 00:52:35.020
Yeah, just there.
对，就在那儿。

1219
00:52:35.380 --> 00:52:38.060
Are you feeling like Aunt Shirley wouldn't have had a Weber grill?
你觉得雪莉阿姨不应该有一个韦伯烤炉吗？

1220
00:52:38.540 --> 00:52:39.480
I don't know.
我不知道。

1221
00:52:39.480 --> 00:52:42.340
It just seems like such random placement.
总觉得这个摆放位置太随意了。

1222
00:52:42.920 --> 00:52:43.340
Hmm.
嗯。

1223
00:52:43.580 --> 00:52:46.320
I wonder if there was like a little Weber grill deal or something.
我在想是不是有什么韦伯烤炉的赞助合作之类的。

1224
00:52:46.900 --> 00:52:47.860
It's not on a porch.
它不在门廊上。

1225
00:52:47.860 --> 00:52:50.040
It's not anywhere where it looks like you would use it.
它不在任何看起来你会使用它的地方。

1226
00:52:50.160 --> 00:52:53.060
It's just tucked on the side of the wall of like a shed.
它只是塞在某个像棚子一样的墙边。

1227
00:52:53.260 --> 00:52:53.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

1228
00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:57.780
I just, every time I watched the talking heads, all I could think about was the Weber grill.
我只是，每次我看访谈镜头时，满脑子想的都是那个韦伯烤炉。

1229
00:52:58.060 --> 00:53:00.520
The Weber grill is really near and dear to my heart.
这个韦伯烤炉真的让我感到非常亲切。

1230
00:53:00.680 --> 00:53:02.300
My dad grills on a Weber grill.
我爸爸就用韦伯烤炉烧烤。

1231
00:53:02.440 --> 00:53:03.980
My dad had one for years.
我爸爸有一个用了很多年。

1232
00:53:04.380 --> 00:53:07.000
Well, this is, I think now, clear why you spotted it.
好吧，我想现在很清楚为什么你能一眼看到了。

1233
00:53:07.120 --> 00:53:07.840
Maybe so.
也许吧。

1234
00:53:08.000 --> 00:53:08.420
I missed it.
我没注意到。

1235
00:53:08.880 --> 00:53:11.100
Well, Dwight is going to tell Fannie and Jeb, you know what?
好吧，德怀特打算对芬妮和杰布说，你知道吗？

1236
00:53:11.200 --> 00:53:12.360
We should do this.
我们应该这么做。

1237
00:53:12.700 --> 00:53:13.420
We should.
我们应该这样做。

1238
00:53:13.580 --> 00:53:15.240
And Fannie's like, I'm sorry, Dwight.
然后芬妮就说，对不起，德怀特。

1239
00:53:15.240 --> 00:53:20.120
But, you know, a farm wife lacks the sophistication that she's used to.
但是，你知道，一个农场主妇缺乏她所习惯的那种精致。

1240
00:53:20.540 --> 00:53:20.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1241
00:53:21.300 --> 00:53:21.620
Yeah.
对。

1242
00:53:21.740 --> 00:53:25.460
She says there's a sort of willing ignorance to the men.
她说男人们有一种刻意的无知。

1243
00:53:26.040 --> 00:53:27.840
And then she has a talking head.
然后她有了一个访谈镜头。

1244
00:53:27.980 --> 00:53:29.060
She's on the porch swing.
她坐在门廊的秋千上。

1245
00:53:29.280 --> 00:53:33.200
It was very funny to me because she's like, I have written some poetry.
这对我来说非常搞笑，因为她说，我写了一些诗。

1246
00:53:33.380 --> 00:53:34.140
Thanks for asking.
谢谢你问起。

1247
00:53:34.400 --> 00:53:34.680
Yeah.
对。

1248
00:53:34.820 --> 00:53:36.960
I actually had a poem recently published.
我其实最近有一首诗发表了。

1249
00:53:37.220 --> 00:53:38.140
Oh, do I have it?
哦，我身上带着吗？

1250
00:53:38.200 --> 00:53:38.640
Yes, I do.
是的，我带着。

1251
00:53:38.640 --> 00:53:39.360
Here it is.
给你。

1252
00:53:39.520 --> 00:53:45.540
It's from the HartfordWomensLitQuarterly.com, and it is titled A Willing Ignorance by Fannie
这篇来自 HartfordWomensLitQuarterly.com，标题是《自愿的无知》，作者是范妮

1253
00:53:45.540 --> 00:53:46.140
Schrute.
·施鲁特。

1254
00:53:47.020 --> 00:53:51.680
Lady, I paused on it, and I tried to, what do you call that, make it bigger?
女士们，我看到这停下了，我试着，你们叫那个什么来着，放大？

1255
00:53:51.880 --> 00:53:52.220
Yes.
对。

1256
00:53:52.560 --> 00:53:53.520
I took a picture.
我截了个图。

1257
00:53:53.780 --> 00:53:54.120
Same.
一样。

1258
00:53:54.220 --> 00:53:54.760
I looked.
我看了。

1259
00:53:54.940 --> 00:53:55.280
Same.
一样。

1260
00:53:55.380 --> 00:53:56.840
I really wanted to read her poem.
我真的很想读读她的诗。

1261
00:53:57.020 --> 00:53:58.000
I really did, too.
我也是，真的。

1262
00:53:58.180 --> 00:54:03.100
And so I went to the writer's notes for this episode, and I found it.
于是我翻了这集的编剧笔记，然后我找到了。

1263
00:54:03.180 --> 00:54:03.980
You did not.
才没有。

1264
00:54:04.160 --> 00:54:04.640
I did.
我找到了。

1265
00:54:05.120 --> 00:54:07.380
We're going to hear Fannie's poem right now.
我们现在就要听听范妮的诗了。

1266
00:54:07.460 --> 00:54:08.360
We sure are.
那是当然。

1267
00:54:08.620 --> 00:54:09.540
Okay, I can't wait.
好吧，我都等不及了。

1268
00:54:09.700 --> 00:54:12.520
Here it is, A Willing Ignorance by Fannie Schrute.
就是这首，范妮·施鲁特写的《自愿的无知》。

1269
00:54:12.720 --> 00:54:17.320
The men I meet are nearly completely ignorant of all things worthwhile.
我遇到的男人对所有有价值的事物都一无所知。

1270
00:54:17.940 --> 00:54:23.720
Whether current events or the classics, these gents think well-read is a lipstick shade for
不论是时事还是经典，这些男士以为“博览群书”是女人的口红色号

1271
00:54:23.720 --> 00:54:24.740
a lady's smile.
涂在微笑上。

1272
00:54:25.120 --> 00:54:25.520
Oh.
哦。

1273
00:54:25.760 --> 00:54:30.300
Their libraries consist of the Bible, of course, but it doesn't avert them from sin.
他们的藏书当然只有《圣经》，但这并不能阻止他们作恶。

1274
00:54:30.300 --> 00:54:35.840
The only way I'd describe them as holy is if they flashed me their toothless grin.
若说他们有什么神圣的地方，那只能是他们露出没牙的傻笑时。

1275
00:54:36.220 --> 00:54:40.980
The men I meet are so patriotic, their minds are like the national debt.
我遇到的男人如此爱国，他们的脑子就像国债一样庞大。

1276
00:54:41.360 --> 00:54:46.840
But if what they say about ignorance is true, they are as blissful as one can get.
但如果他们对无知的理解属实，那他们该是世上最幸福的人了。

1277
00:54:47.500 --> 00:54:48.020
Wow.
哇。

1278
00:54:48.460 --> 00:54:49.860
Fannie was holding on to it a lot.
范妮憋了挺久了。

1279
00:54:50.160 --> 00:54:53.280
This does not sound like a woman who's going to want to come back to this farm.
这听起来可不像是一个还想回这个农场来的女人。

1280
00:54:53.460 --> 00:54:54.120
Does not.
确实不像。

1281
00:54:54.120 --> 00:54:58.900
But, well, listen, Jeb also doesn't want to come back to the farm.
不过，听着，杰布也不想回农场。

1282
00:54:59.060 --> 00:55:03.240
He says people here are like a fart, which I guess is another way to put it.
他说这里的人就像个屁，我想这是另一种表达方式吧。

1283
00:55:03.400 --> 00:55:06.040
Then he makes a fart noise in case you're not sure what a fart is.
然后他模仿了一个放屁的声音，以防你不知道屁是什么样。

1284
00:55:06.220 --> 00:55:06.480
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1285
00:55:07.060 --> 00:55:07.960
Dwight says, you know what?
德怀特说，你知道吗？

1286
00:55:08.020 --> 00:55:10.960
Why don't you guys stay for a few nights and then decide?
你们为什么不留下来住几个晚上再做决定呢？

1287
00:55:11.560 --> 00:55:12.200
Zeke is in.
泽克同意了。

1288
00:55:12.760 --> 00:55:13.980
Zeke is like, I'll do it.
泽克就像是，我来吧。

1289
00:55:14.680 --> 00:55:18.880
He has a talking head where he said, you know, it really wasn't easy growing up with Dwight
他有一个单独采访镜头说，你知道，跟德怀特

1290
00:55:18.880 --> 00:55:24.960
and Moe's because Dwight is obviously the cool one and Moe's was the visionary and that
和莫斯一起长大真不容易，因为德怀特显然是那个酷的人，莫斯是那个有远见的人，而

1291
00:55:24.960 --> 00:55:26.420
left him to be the comedian.
这就把他留作搞笑担当了。

1292
00:55:26.880 --> 00:55:29.420
Thirteen minutes, twenty-one seconds, Blue Weber grill.
十三分二十一秒，韦伯蓝色烤架。

1293
00:55:29.840 --> 00:55:30.520
There it is.
就是它。

1294
00:55:30.620 --> 00:55:31.200
There it is.
就是这样。

1295
00:55:31.780 --> 00:55:36.500
Somehow Dwight is going to charm Fannie into agreeing to stay a few days.
不知怎么的，德怀特要施展魅力让范妮同意留下来几天。

1296
00:55:36.660 --> 00:55:38.940
By counting incorrectly in French.
通过用法语数错数。

1297
00:55:39.500 --> 00:55:39.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1298
00:55:40.260 --> 00:55:40.400
Yeah.
对。

1299
00:55:40.580 --> 00:55:45.200
But they have a laugh and like a little Russell sibling thing on the couch and she's like,
但他们一起笑了，就像沙发上的拉塞尔兄妹那样，然后她说，

1300
00:55:45.300 --> 00:55:45.840
okay, fine.
好吧，行吧。

1301
00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:46.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1302
00:55:46.700 --> 00:55:50.120
Well, lady, you know, I told you I had a few things for my digital clutter.
好吧，女士，你知道的，我告诉过你我有些关于清理数码杂物的事情要处理。

1303
00:55:50.360 --> 00:55:50.660
Yeah.
对。

1304
00:55:50.780 --> 00:55:51.500
I've shared two.
我已经分享了两个。

1305
00:55:51.680 --> 00:55:51.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1306
00:55:52.080 --> 00:55:53.200
Here's my last one.
这是我的最后一个。

1307
00:55:53.300 --> 00:55:53.520
Okay.
好的。

1308
00:55:53.880 --> 00:55:58.520
We know that you and I were trying to figure out what we were going to do with this time
我们知道你和我当时在琢磨这段休假时间

1309
00:55:58.520 --> 00:55:58.840
off.
要做点什么。

1310
00:55:59.100 --> 00:55:59.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1311
00:55:59.580 --> 00:56:01.400
I'm trying to get to Texas with Isabel.
我正打算和伊莎贝尔去得克萨斯州。

1312
00:56:01.600 --> 00:56:01.780
Yep.
没错。

1313
00:56:01.940 --> 00:56:02.720
And I got there.
而我做到了。

1314
00:56:02.900 --> 00:56:03.660
Oh, nice.
哦，太棒了。

1315
00:56:03.880 --> 00:56:06.540
And you emailed me, here's what I'm doing.
然后你给我发了一封邮件，说这就是我在做的事。

1316
00:56:06.740 --> 00:56:07.500
What did I do?
我做了什么？

1317
00:56:07.620 --> 00:56:09.540
You titled the email, Puttering.
你给邮件起标题叫“瞎忙活”。

1318
00:56:10.520 --> 00:56:14.020
And you said, today is fantasy football day.
你说，今天是梦幻足球日。

1319
00:56:14.020 --> 00:56:17.300
We are both in our jerseys and we are puttering together.
我们都穿着球衣，一起在家里东摸摸西弄弄。

1320
00:56:17.600 --> 00:56:19.780
We just cleaned out the basket by the door.
我们刚清理完门边的篮子。

1321
00:56:19.980 --> 00:56:20.860
I'm in heaven.
我简直置身天堂。

1322
00:56:21.260 --> 00:56:26.840
And attached was the cutest photo of you and your baby son in matching jerseys, looking at
附件是一张超级可爱的照片，你和你婴儿时期的儿子穿着情侣球衣，互相看着

1323
00:56:26.840 --> 00:56:27.920
each other and laughing.
并且大笑。

1324
00:56:28.400 --> 00:56:28.920
Aw.
噢。

1325
00:56:28.920 --> 00:56:33.480
And I wrote back and said, I love everything about this photo.
我回信说，我喜欢这张照片的一切。

1326
00:56:34.160 --> 00:56:35.480
And I have it.
而且我留着它呢。

1327
00:56:35.580 --> 00:56:36.300
You want to see it?
你想看吗？

1328
00:56:36.320 --> 00:56:36.380
What?
什么？

1329
00:56:36.440 --> 00:56:36.720
Yes.
想。

1330
00:56:36.980 --> 00:56:37.220
You do?
真的吗？

1331
00:56:37.480 --> 00:56:38.400
Oh, I'm going to cry.
哦，我要哭了。

1332
00:56:38.740 --> 00:56:39.160
I know.
我知道。

1333
00:56:39.300 --> 00:56:41.160
It is the sweetest thing, lady.
这真的是最甜蜜的事了，女士。

1334
00:56:41.280 --> 00:56:42.460
You were so happy.
你当时太幸福了。

1335
00:56:42.680 --> 00:56:45.240
Well, this kid's about to turn 13, so.
好吧，这孩子快13岁了，所以。

1336
00:56:45.360 --> 00:56:48.140
Oh, this is just going to cue the waterworks.
哦，这简直要让人泪奔了。

1337
00:56:48.280 --> 00:56:48.440
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1338
00:56:49.280 --> 00:56:50.040
Let me see.
让我看看。

1339
00:56:50.100 --> 00:56:50.940
This is precious.
太珍贵了。

1340
00:56:52.740 --> 00:56:54.340
Stop it now.
别这样。

1341
00:56:54.560 --> 00:56:54.800
Yep.
没错。

1342
00:56:55.380 --> 00:56:56.260
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1343
00:56:56.380 --> 00:56:56.740
All right.
好了。

1344
00:56:56.940 --> 00:56:59.580
You know I don't often share pictures of my kiddos.
你知道我平时不怎么分享我孩子们的照片。

1345
00:56:59.700 --> 00:57:00.140
I know.
我知道。

1346
00:57:00.280 --> 00:57:02.600
But you can put this one on Office Ladies Pod.
但你可以把这张发到“办公室女士”播客上。

1347
00:57:03.060 --> 00:57:04.320
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

1348
00:57:04.320 --> 00:57:07.400
That's what you were doing with your day off during the farm.
这就是你放假那天在农场时做的事。

1349
00:57:07.980 --> 00:57:09.940
Oh, I love to putter.
哦，我最喜欢东摸摸西弄弄了。

1350
00:57:10.140 --> 00:57:10.680
I know.
我知道。

1351
00:57:12.160 --> 00:57:17.600
So sometimes, folks, it's a good thing that you don't clean out your email inbox for years.
所以有时候，各位，多年不清理电子邮箱收件箱其实是一件好事。

1352
00:57:18.180 --> 00:57:20.960
I am so grateful you don't clean out your email inbox.
我太庆幸你没有清理电子邮箱收件箱了。

1353
00:57:22.200 --> 00:57:24.920
So now we are on the back porch.
所以现在我们在后廊。

1354
00:57:25.420 --> 00:57:31.880
Esther, Zeke, and others are performing the song Sons and Daughters by the Decembrists.
埃丝特、齐克和其他人正在演奏Decemberists乐队的歌曲《Sons and Daughters》。

1355
00:57:32.400 --> 00:57:34.820
We had a fan question from Grace F.
我们收到了来自北爱尔兰贝尔法斯特的格蕾丝·F的粉丝提问，

1356
00:57:34.980 --> 00:57:37.100
in Belfast, Northern Ireland, who said,
她说，

1357
00:57:37.260 --> 00:57:41.720
Please tell me everything about how the song Sons and Daughters by the Decembrists came to be picked.
请告诉我关于这首由Decemberists演唱的《Sons and Daughters》是如何被选中的所有故事。

1358
00:57:41.740 --> 00:57:44.800
I absolutely love this and often listen to it on YouTube.
我超级喜欢这首歌，经常在YouTube上听。

1359
00:57:45.040 --> 00:57:48.860
I think the rendition that Dwight and his family do on the steps is just perfect.
我觉得德怀特和他的家人在台阶上的演绎简直完美。

1360
00:57:48.860 --> 00:57:51.460
It's just a pity that it doesn't go on longer.
只可惜没有放得更长一点。

1361
00:57:51.780 --> 00:57:54.940
Well, Grace, this song was in the original script.
好吧，格蕾丝，这首歌在最初的剧本里就有。

1362
00:57:55.280 --> 00:57:56.160
It was Paul's idea.
这是保罗的主意。

1363
00:57:56.300 --> 00:57:57.620
He loves this song.
他很喜欢这首歌。

1364
00:57:57.960 --> 00:58:03.920
And crazy enough, Rainn Wilson knew Colin Malloy from having done a promotional video
说来也巧，雷恩·威尔逊认识科林·马拉伊，因为他曾为科林写的一本书

1365
00:58:03.920 --> 00:58:07.400
for a book that Colin wrote, and they had become friends.
拍过宣传视频，两人由此成为了朋友。

1366
00:58:08.060 --> 00:58:11.380
I texted Rainn about this, and he actually said Colin is, quote,
我为此给雷恩发了短信，他居然说科林是，引述一下，

1367
00:58:11.480 --> 00:58:12.700
my brother from another mother.
我异父异母的兄弟。

1368
00:58:12.940 --> 00:58:15.720
And he asked Colin if we could use the song on the show.
他还问科林我们是否可以在剧里使用这首歌。

1369
00:58:15.720 --> 00:58:20.360
Steve Burgess said it cost $15,000, and I thought maybe we'd like to hear.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说这要花15000美元，我想也许大家会想听听。

1370
00:58:20.800 --> 00:58:24.320
Lady, I loved it, too, and I also wanted to play it.
女士，我也很喜欢，而且我也很想放这首歌。

1371
00:58:24.620 --> 00:58:25.000
All right.
好吧。

1372
00:58:25.100 --> 00:58:25.780
Here it is.
就是这个。

1373
00:58:53.740 --> 00:58:55.180
Well, I have to say this.
嗯，我得说这个。

1374
00:58:55.280 --> 00:58:57.500
Paul Lieberstein has really good taste in music.
保罗·利伯斯坦的音乐品味真的很好。

1375
00:58:57.620 --> 00:58:58.000
He does.
确实如此。

1376
00:58:58.000 --> 00:59:02.180
Because I'm definitely liking, like, the musicality of this pilot.
因为我真的很喜欢这个试播集的音乐感。

1377
00:59:02.540 --> 00:59:03.360
The soundtrack.
原声带。

1378
00:59:03.660 --> 00:59:04.680
Yes, exactly.
对，完全正确。

1379
00:59:05.160 --> 00:59:08.080
Well, you guys all saw Nora playing the accordion in this scene,
好了，大家都在这场戏里看到诺拉在拉手风琴了，

1380
00:59:08.100 --> 00:59:10.260
and she plays the accordion in real life.
她现实生活中也会拉手风琴。

1381
00:59:10.260 --> 00:59:14.220
We mentioned that earlier, and we asked her about playing it in this episode.
我们刚才提到了这一点，并问了她在这集里演奏的事。

1382
00:59:14.400 --> 00:59:17.380
She said it was a very last-minute addition.
她说这是一个非常临时候补的安排。

1383
00:59:17.700 --> 00:59:23.060
She said Paul only realized that she was in Edward Sharp and the Magnetic Zeros
她说保罗直到拍摄这场戏的前一晚，才意识到

1384
00:59:23.060 --> 00:59:27.000
and that she played accordion the night before they shot this scene.
她曾加入爱德华·夏普与磁性零点乐队，并且她会拉手风琴。

1385
00:59:27.160 --> 00:59:31.380
He called her up and asked her if she would play a song with some of the other farm castmates.
他打电话给她，问她愿不愿意和其他农场演员一起弹唱一首歌。

1386
00:59:31.620 --> 00:59:35.420
She also said she'd been playing music with Matt Jones for years already,
她还说她和马特·琼斯已经一起玩音乐好几年了，

1387
00:59:35.420 --> 00:59:39.900
so it was just a real joy to work out the song in their trailers before they shot.
所以在拍摄前能在他们的房车里合练这首歌真的非常开心。

1388
00:59:40.160 --> 00:59:43.840
She said she remembers going back and forth with him about which key to do it in.
她说她记得自己和他在究竟用哪个调子弹唱这事上讨论了好几次。

1389
00:59:44.220 --> 00:59:47.600
One was better for her, one was better for him, and she said he won.
一个调对她比较好，另一个对他比较好，而她说他赢了。

1390
00:59:48.260 --> 00:59:49.120
That's very funny.
太有趣了。

1391
00:59:49.180 --> 00:59:50.660
I think they sound fantastic.
我觉得他们听起来棒极了。

1392
00:59:50.860 --> 00:59:51.440
I do, too.
我也这么觉得。

1393
00:59:51.720 --> 00:59:53.840
I think we should hear them sing it at the end.
我觉得我们应该在最后听听他们唱。

1394
00:59:53.840 --> 00:59:54.680
Oh, yes!
哦，太好了！

1395
00:59:54.860 --> 00:59:55.940
I love that idea.
我喜欢这个主意。

1396
00:59:56.280 --> 01:00:03.020
Well, as this jam session continues, Dwight is going to lay two little black things in front of Esther.
好了，随着这场即兴演奏的继续，德怀特要在埃丝特面前放下两样黑色的小东西。

1397
01:00:03.720 --> 01:00:06.920
Fanny notices this, and she says,
芬妮注意到了这一点，她说道，

1398
01:00:07.120 --> 01:00:09.920
Oh, yes, I forgot about this old custom.
哦，对了，我都忘了这个旧习俗了。

1399
01:00:10.300 --> 01:00:14.800
If a man wants to court a woman, he'll throw the beaks of a crow at her,
如果一个男人想向女人求爱，他会把乌鸦的嘴扔向她，

1400
01:00:14.960 --> 01:00:18.680
and if she's interested, she must destroy the beaks.
如果她有兴趣，就必须毁掉这些鸟嘴。

1401
01:00:18.680 --> 01:00:25.660
Yes, I would like to point out that during all of this sort of front porch time,
是的，我想指出的是，在所有这些前廊闲聊的时间里，

1402
01:00:26.020 --> 01:00:28.640
Dwight looks like an Eddie Bauer catalog model.
德怀特看起来就像是一个艾迪·鲍尔的目录模特。

1403
01:00:29.120 --> 01:00:30.200
Did you think so?
你觉得是吗？

1404
01:00:30.300 --> 01:00:31.060
I did think so.
我是这么觉得的。

1405
01:00:31.340 --> 01:00:34.140
In fact, during his talking head at 13 minutes 58 seconds,
事实上，在他在13分58秒的访谈镜头里，

