Please, please, look at Dwight's overalls in this scene when he's standing next to Fanny's
拜托，拜托，看看这场戏里德怀特站在范妮车

1717
01:13:47.340 --> 01:13:47.620
car.
旁时的背带裤。

1718
01:13:47.880 --> 01:13:49.820
These have never been worn before.
这绝对是没穿过的。

1719
01:13:50.100 --> 01:13:51.900
Not for a hot second.
一秒钟都没有。

1720
01:13:52.160 --> 01:13:57.740
These are brand new, shiny denim, stiff overalls.
这是全新的、闪亮的牛仔布、硬挺的背带裤。

1721
01:13:57.860 --> 01:14:00.060
They have never seen a day's work on the farm.
它们在农场里连一天农活都没干过。

1722
01:14:00.640 --> 01:14:03.200
This is my overalls bullsh** card.
这是我的背带裤胡扯牌。

1723
01:14:03.400 --> 01:14:05.320
Played like a true farm girl.
真不愧是个地道的农场女孩。

1724
01:14:05.600 --> 01:14:06.240
Thank you.
谢谢。

1725
01:14:06.680 --> 01:14:09.240
Just get a pair of old overalls already.
赶紧去买条旧背带裤吧。

1726
01:14:09.860 --> 01:14:11.860
Well, guess what?
好吧，你猜怎么着？

1727
01:14:12.260 --> 01:14:15.180
Dwight, Fanny, and Jeb, they're standing together.
德怀特、范妮和杰布，他们站在一起。

1728
01:14:15.620 --> 01:14:17.300
They're looking at their new farm.
他们看着他们的新农场。

1729
01:14:17.680 --> 01:14:21.860
It's going to take a lot of work to man this land, but they're up for it.
要经营这片土地需要付出很多努力，但他们已经准备好了。

1730
01:14:22.100 --> 01:14:23.420
Dwight says, I'll do it.
德怀特说，我来干。

1731
01:14:23.600 --> 01:14:23.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1732
01:14:24.160 --> 01:14:24.380
Yep.
没错。

1733
01:14:24.580 --> 01:14:26.000
And that's the end of the episode.
这就是这一集的结尾。

1734
01:14:26.680 --> 01:14:31.680
A big thank you to Steve Burgess, Rainn Wilson, and of course, Nora Kirkpatrick.
非常感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯、雷恩·威尔森，当然还有诺拉·柯克帕特里克。

1735
01:14:32.280 --> 01:14:37.460
Everyone, Nora just made her first feature that she wrote and directed, starring Alexandra
各位，诺拉刚刚完成了她自编自导的第一部故事片，由亚历山大

1736
01:14:37.460 --> 01:14:43.040
Daddario, Josh Gad, David Diggs, and Ashley Park that should be coming out soon, she says.
达达里奥、乔什·加德、戴维·迪格斯和阿什利·帕克主演，她表示该片应该很快就会上映。

1737
01:14:43.240 --> 01:14:47.760
It's called A Tree Fell in the Woods, and she just finished writing on a new show for
这部电影名叫《树倒林中》，她刚刚为亚马逊的一部新剧

1738
01:14:47.760 --> 01:14:49.120
Amazon called The Runarounds.
《The Runarounds》完成了编剧工作。

1739
01:14:49.180 --> 01:14:50.460
It'll be out early next year.
该剧将于明年初上线。

1740
01:14:50.860 --> 01:14:54.920
It's about a young rock band, and she said she thinks the show is going to be very special.
它讲述了一个年轻摇滚乐队的故事，她说她觉得这部剧会非常特别。

1741
01:14:55.400 --> 01:14:59.100
You know, she was one of the writers of the show Daisy Jones and the Six.
要知道，她也是电视剧《黛西与乐队》的编剧之一。

1742
01:14:59.440 --> 01:15:00.740
She's so talented.
她太有才了。

1743
01:15:01.080 --> 01:15:01.460
I know.
我懂的。

1744
01:15:02.040 --> 01:15:03.340
Nora, thank you so much.
诺拉，非常感谢你。

1745
01:15:03.760 --> 01:15:05.320
Yes, Nora, thank you so much.
是的，诺拉，非常感谢你。

1746
01:15:05.500 --> 01:15:08.600
And thank you guys for sending in your questions and your comments.
也谢谢大家发来你们的问题和评论。

1747
01:15:08.980 --> 01:15:10.800
We love doing this podcaSt.
我们很喜欢做这个播客。

1748
01:15:10.860 --> 01:15:13.500
We're so thrilled that Sam and Cassie are back.
我们很高兴萨姆和卡西回来了。

1749
01:15:13.760 --> 01:15:16.260
Sam, any words before we sign off?
萨姆，在我们结束之前有什么想说的吗？

1750
01:15:16.780 --> 01:15:17.460
Yes, I do.
是的，我有。

1751
01:15:17.700 --> 01:15:20.340
One, Angela, you have to stop saying laying pipe.
第一，安吉拉，你得别再说什么“铺管道”了。

1752
01:15:20.460 --> 01:15:21.260
That's not what that means.
那根本不是那个意思。

1753
01:15:21.380 --> 01:15:22.640
It is what it means, Sam.
那就是那个意思，萨姆。

1754
01:15:22.640 --> 01:15:23.860
It's a writer's term.
这是个编剧术语。

1755
01:15:23.860 --> 01:15:24.600
No, it's not.
不，根本不是。

1756
01:15:25.080 --> 01:15:25.720
It is.
就是。

1757
01:15:25.840 --> 01:15:26.460
It's both.
两个意思都有。

1758
01:15:26.680 --> 01:15:28.000
We looked it up, Sam.
我们查过了，萨姆。

1759
01:15:28.100 --> 01:15:28.540
We had to look it up, Sam.
我们不得不去查一下，萨姆。

1760
01:15:28.540 --> 01:15:34.040
Because I said the same thing, and we did look it up, and it is something that writers
因为我也说过同样的话，而且我们确实查了，这确实是编剧

1761
01:15:34.040 --> 01:15:35.200
use for script.
在剧本里用的词。

1762
01:15:35.240 --> 01:15:36.340
We did Google it.
我们确实谷歌过了。

1763
01:15:36.520 --> 01:15:38.500
But it does also mean something else.
但它也确实有别的意思。

1764
01:15:38.660 --> 01:15:41.300
Thank you, Sam, for reminding us.
谢谢你，萨姆，提醒了我们。

1765
01:15:41.500 --> 01:15:42.440
That and I just—
再加上我刚刚——

1766
01:15:42.440 --> 01:15:43.360
Don't Google it, everybody.
大家千万别去谷歌。

1767
01:15:43.560 --> 01:15:43.780
Yes.
没错。

1768
01:15:43.940 --> 01:15:49.360
I just want to give a massive thanks to the fans of the show who reached out with support
我只想向那些在我被解雇时

1769
01:15:49.360 --> 01:15:50.640
when I was laid off.
伸出援手、给予支持的剧迷们表达由衷的感谢。

1770
01:15:50.640 --> 01:15:55.380
It got back to me, the amount of support you sent, and it really, really meant a lot.
你们发来的支持我都收到了，真的、真的意义重大。

1771
01:15:55.480 --> 01:15:57.840
I feel like I was able to attend my own funeral.
我感觉就像是去参加了自己的葬礼一样。

1772
01:15:58.660 --> 01:16:00.220
Aw, I know what you mean.
噢，我懂你的意思。

1773
01:16:00.520 --> 01:16:00.680
Yeah.
对。

1774
01:16:00.680 --> 01:16:01.640
I just want to say this.
我只想说这个。

1775
01:16:01.780 --> 01:16:05.400
I highly recommend to anybody out there who's working, get fired.
我强烈建议正在上班的任何人，去被解雇一次。

1776
01:16:05.760 --> 01:16:07.160
Have a going-away party.
办个欢送派对。

1777
01:16:07.300 --> 01:16:08.800
Have all your coworkers cry.
让所有的同事都为你哭泣。

1778
01:16:09.220 --> 01:16:10.340
Get a severance package.
拿一笔离职补偿金。

1779
01:16:10.520 --> 01:16:11.840
Go to Europe for a couple weeks.
去欧洲玩上几个星期。

1780
01:16:11.840 --> 01:16:16.520
And just when you're thinking about how you're going to be able to pay rent, go back to work.
就在你琢磨着该怎么交房租的时候，回去上班。

1781
01:16:16.960 --> 01:16:21.740
It's the ideal career path, and I just want to say thanks to everyone.
这是最理想的职业发展道路，我只想对大家说声谢谢。

1782
01:16:21.980 --> 01:16:22.280
Aw.
噢。

1783
01:16:22.840 --> 01:16:25.920
Well, I am just so excited about this new chapter.
总之，我对这个全新的篇章感到无比兴奋。

1784
01:16:26.180 --> 01:16:29.360
A big thank you to Odyssey for being our new partner.
非常感谢奥德赛成为我们的新合作伙伴。

1785
01:16:29.560 --> 01:16:30.000
Yes.
是的。

1786
01:16:30.220 --> 01:16:31.140
We are thrilled.
我们激动不已。

1787
01:16:31.360 --> 01:16:34.700
We are so happy, and we hope you guys have a great week.
我们太高兴了，希望大家这周过得愉快。

1788
01:16:34.700 --> 01:16:41.260
We are going to see you next week, and I think we've got to hear Nora and the cast singing
我们下周见，我想我们得听听诺拉和演员们合唱的

1789
01:16:41.260 --> 01:16:42.200
Sons and Daughters.
《儿女们》。

1790
01:16:42.400 --> 01:16:43.400
I like that idea.
我喜欢这个主意。

1791
01:16:44.020 --> 01:16:48.540
Sons and Daughters will make our homes on the wall.
《儿女们》将在我们心头筑起家园。

1792
01:16:48.560 --> 01:17:07.040
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

